ttribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "22464"] "category" "local_authored" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/repairs.json" "file_sha256" "0328005daa91919dd8bb81fd729228440954ec812e808e91c99da77efc57aee9" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "571ee7e4f8997fdfae74f800edd84d0efce760607b5043aa85a8d9d81962095f" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/verification.json" "basis" 653} {"question" "q-288826" "field" "answer" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "− 22464"] "category" "local_authored" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/repairs.json" "file_sha256" "0328005daa91919dd8bb81fd729228440954ec812e808e91c99da77efc57aee9" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "571ee7e4f8997fdfae74f800edd84d0efce760607b5043aa85a8d9d81962095f" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/verification.json" "basis" 653}] "sources" [{"question" "q-288103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic coefficient of a particular quadratic equation equals $3.$ The sum of the solutions equals $4,$ and the product of the solutions equals $-5.$ Find the equation.\n\nThe equation is\n{{field-1}}\n$=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's use the given information to determine the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ in this case:\n\n- We're told that the quadratic coefficient equals $3.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\na=3.\n$$\n\n- We're told that the sum of the roots equals $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =-\\frac{b}{a} \\\\ 4 & =-\\frac{b}{3} \\\\ -12 & =b \\\\ b & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- We're told that the product of the roots equals $-5.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5 & =\\frac{c}{a} \\\\ -5 & =\\frac{c}{3} \\\\ -15 & =c \\\\ c & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation has coefficients\n\n$$\na=3,\\,b=-12,\\,c=-15\n$$\n\nand the equation is\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}-12x-15=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a76d3573aef6584c14d7f0db3fc83fe38552285a279043eaef946ff4f853f12"} {"question" "q-288103" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288103" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x^2-12x-15"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the quadratic equation\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+7x-27=0.\n$$\n\n**Without** solving the equation, determine the product of its solutions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nFor the given quadratic equation, we have\n\n$$\na=9,\\,b=7,\\,c=-27.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the product of the solutions is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{a} & =\\frac{(-27)}{9}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a76d3573aef6584c14d7f0db3fc83fe38552285a279043eaef946ff4f853f12"} {"question" "q-288815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{9}"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the quadratic equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+68x-1\\,041=0.\n$$\n\n**Without** solving the equation, determine the product of its solutions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nFor the given quadratic equation, we have\n\n$$\na=1,\\,b=68,\\,c=-1\\,041.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the product of the solutions is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{a} & =\\frac{(-1\\,041)}{1}=-1\\,041.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a76d3573aef6584c14d7f0db3fc83fe38552285a279043eaef946ff4f853f12"} {"question" "q-288826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2)\\cdot 1\\,041"] ["math" "-1\\,041"] ["math" "1\\,041"] ["math" "\\frac{-1\\,041}{68}"] ["math" "\\frac{68}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1\\,041"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic coefficient of a particular quadratic equation equals $4.$ The sum of the solutions equals $-9,$ and the product of the solutions equals $10.$ Find the equation.\n\nThe equation is\n{{field-1}}  \n$=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's use the given information to determine the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ in this case:\n\n- We're told that the quadratic coefficient equals $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\na=4.\n$$\n\n- We're told that the sum of the roots equals $-9.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9 & =-\\frac{b}{a} \\\\ -9 & =-\\frac{b}{4} \\\\ 36 & =b \\\\ b & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- We're told that the product of the roots equals $10.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =\\frac{c}{a} \\\\ 10 & =\\frac{c}{4} \\\\ 40 & =c \\\\ c & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation has coefficients\n\n$$\na=4,\\,b=36,\\,c=40\n$$\n\nand the equation is\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+36x+40=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a76d3573aef6584c14d7f0db3fc83fe38552285a279043eaef946ff4f853f12"} {"question" "q-288828" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288828" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x^2+36x+40"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic coefficient of a particular quadratic equation equals $1.$ The sum of the solutions equals $7,$ and the product of the solutions equals $12.$ Find the equation.\n\nThe equation is\n{{field-1}}\n$=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's use the given information to determine the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ in this case:\n\n- We're told that the quadratic coefficient equals $1.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\na=1.\n$$\n\n- We're told that the sum of the roots equals $7.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =-\\frac{b}{a} \\\\ 7 & =-\\frac{b}{1} \\\\ -7 & =b \\\\ b & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- We're told that the product of the roots equals $12.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =\\frac{c}{a} \\\\ 12 & =\\frac{c}{1} \\\\ c & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation has coefficients\n\n$$\na=1,\\,b=-7,\\,c=12\n$$\n\nand the equation is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-7x+12=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a76d3573aef6584c14d7f0db3fc83fe38552285a279043eaef946ff4f853f12"} {"question" "q-288848" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"} {"question" "q-288848" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x^2-7x+12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968742/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e6d9089bd864464bc48c4d17d41e1a9bb7105c8037fd0273c940851d572398a"}] "usage" {"q-288848" [] "q-288826" [] "q-288815" [] "q-288103" []} "basis" 779 "retractions" [[17592186083553 :question/problem "The quadratic coefficient of a particular quadratic equation equals $3$. The sum of the solutions equals $4$, and the product of the solutions equals $-5$. Find the equation.The equation is\n{{field-1}}\n$= 0$.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"deriving-vietas-formulas\"></a>"] [17592186083556 :question/problem "Consider the quadratic equation\n\n$9x^{2} + 7x - 27 = 0$.\n**Without** solving the equation, determine the product of its solutions."] [17592186259313 :question/answer-fields 17592186274612] [17592186083558 :question/problem "The quadratic coefficient of a particular quadratic equation equals $1$. The sum of the